==============================

lmplot's own code (cpp/, schema/, scripts/, examples/, tests; including the
vendored `cpp/dslvm.hpp` runtime from the cpp-dsl-sdk project and the deflate
encoder from lmcad) is Copyright (c) 2026 Lattice Systems LLC, MIT license (see
LICENSE). This file covers third-party components shipped in or linked into the
distributed binaries. `lmplot --notices` prints it.

gnuplot
-------
Statically linked into every lmplot binary (about 60 source files of gnuplot
6.1.0-dev, https://github.com/gnuplot/gnuplot, pinned in gnuplot.lock). The
gnuplot license permits distributing binaries built from modified sources
provided the modifications are distributed as patches, the version is marked,
and the contact information is retained. lmplot does all three:

  - Modifications: the files in `patches/` are the complete and only changes
    to the pinned gnuplot source; they ship with every release next to the
    binaries and live at https://github.com/lmctl-ai/lmplot/tree/main/patches.
    That includes patches/0005-lmpng-terminal.patch, lmplot's native PNG
    terminal driver, which follows gnuplot's own terminal drivers and is
    distributed under gnuplot's terms. The rasterizer it calls (cpp/raster) and
    the embedding hook (cpp/lmplot_embed.inc) are lmplot's own MIT code.
  - Version identification: this build identifies itself as "lmplot" (see
    `lmplot --version`; `show version` reports the lmplot patch level).
  - Contact: for problems with this modified version write to
    https://github.com/lmctl-ai/lmplot/issues (Lattice Systems LLC). Contact
    information for the base software is retained below and in the gnuplot
    sources.

